# Frequently Asked Questions

Use this page for orientation. Follow the linked guide when you need the full contract.

## What is Rocci?

Rocci is an experimental toolchain for writing HTML interfaces in Roc. `.rocci` templates lower to ordinary Roc; standalone server declarations can produce HTTP applications. Start with [the stack](/docs/the-stack/).

## Is Rocci a client-side JavaScript framework?

No. Rocci renders semantic HTML from Roc. Interactive applications can use Datastar as a browser transport for requests, HTML patches, commands, and shared streams; durable state remains on the server. Read [Handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/).

## When should I use `.rocci` or `.rocdown`?

Use `.rocci` when view structure and Roc logic lead. Use `.rocdown` when prose leads, then use `.rocci` for the visible site shell and reusable painters. See [Rocdown pages](/docs/rocdown/pages/).

## Can Rocdown publish interactive pages?

Yes. A hybrid site can publish CDN HTML and run a sibling island service for pages with server handlers. The current v1 path uses existing component and handler declarations; the reserved `@island` syntax is not implemented. See [Publish a hybrid site](/docs/rocdown/hybrid/).

## Can I build desktop applications?

`rocci run` can open a Tao/Wry preview window, and `rocci bundle` can create a local, ad-hoc-signed macOS application bundle. Production signing, installers, updates, and broad native APIs are not shipped. See [Runtime compatibility](/docs/reference/compatibility/).

## Is Rocci ready for production adoption?

Treat it as an active experiment. Evaluate the implemented surface and current limitations in [Project status](/project/status/); do not infer support from an uncited platform or performance claim.
